{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790353085,"nonce":"v3EXJRCR0wede//61gtI2PYG08M=","title":"Macro-time ExprTools missing; `${expr}` splices rejected; expression metadata bound too tightly; getLocalImports unknown","message":"Issue4121: a macro using `using haxe.macro.Tools` calls `e.map(f)` and `e.toString()`, which the interpreter did not know (\"cannot call method 'map' on Expr\"). Its `macro (${e.map(add)})` was rejected (\"unknown dollar identifier\") because `${...}` has an empty kind, which the splice engine did not treat as `$e{...}`. And `@:test x = 1` parsed as `(@:test x) = 1`, while Haxe reads metadata over the whole following expression, `@:test (x = 1)`.\n\nIssue3560: Context.getLocalImports() was unknown. Std.string of an enum value also printed `Enum.Ctor(a, b)` where Haxe prints `Ctor(a,b)`.\n\nFix: ExprTools.map/iter/toString at macro time. toString is macro_system/printer.rs, a case-for-case port of std/haxe/macro/Printer.hx (identical to upstream 4.3.6); 17 probe expressions print byte-identically. `${...}` is `$e{...}`. Expression metadata takes a whole expression. getLocalImports returns ImportExprs, latest first. Context.withImports runs its callback.\n\nConformance 668 -\u003e 671 (Issue4121, Issue3560, Issue11488), 0 LOST. MOVED Issue5039: it now parses as Haxe does, and fails on the unimplemented @:bypassAccessor. Still open: Issue10537 needs withImports's imports and usings in scope for the deferred typeExpr; Issue3387 needs registerFileContents plus positions that carry file and end.","files":null}]}